    "created_at": "2024-03-16T12:58:50Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-03-16T13:02:22Z",
    "body": "But even with `type=\"\"` browsers do not support this and ignore the `<link rel=preload>`. See this example: https://resource-loading-examples.glitch.me/preload-types.html\r\n\r\nIt looks like only these `as` values are supported by the three main browser engines:\r\n- fetch\r\n- image\r\n- font\r\n- script\r\n- style\r\n- track (not supported by Firefox)\r\n\r\nShould we remove the rest from https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#match-preload-type and maybe add a note linking to this to explain only certain resource types can be fetched?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
